.TH DNS_NOTIFY 1 "2026-02-26" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dns_notify \- send a DNS NOTIFY message to a nameserver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dns_notify.py
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fISECS\fR]
[\fB\-\-tcp\fR]
\fIzone\fR \fIserver\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dns_notify
sends a DNS NOTIFY message (RFC\ 1996) to the specified nameserver, requesting
that it check whether the given zone has been updated and initiate a zone
transfer if so.
.PP
The NOTIFY message is a standard DNS query with opcode NOTIFY\ (4) and the
AA\ (Authoritative\ Answer) flag set, carrying a single question record for
the zone with type SOA.
.PP
The target server may be specified as a hostname, a short (unqualified) name,
or an IPv4/IPv6 address. Hostnames are resolved via the system resolver before
the message is sent.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I zone
The DNS zone name to notify (e.g.\&
.BR example.com ).
.TP
.I server
The target nameserver, given as a hostname or IP address.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p \ \fIPORT\fR ", " \-\-port \ \fIPORT\fR
Destination port. Default:
.BR 53 .
.TP
.BR \-t \ \fISECS\fR ", " \-\-timeout \ \fISECS\fR
Seconds to wait for a response before giving up. Default:
.BR 5.0 .
.TP
.B \-\-tcp
Send the NOTIFY message over TCP instead of UDP.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a NOTIFY for
.I example.com
to a nameserver by hostname:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dns_notify.py example.com ns1.example.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Send a NOTIFY using an IP address:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dns_notify.py example.com 192.0.2.53
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use a non-standard port:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dns_notify.py example.com ns1.example.com \-p 5353
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use TCP transport with a 2-second timeout:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dns_notify.py example.com ns1.example.com \-\-tcp \-t 2
.EE
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
On success the resolved server address, port, and response rcode are printed to
standard output.
.PP
.B NOERROR
.RS
The server acknowledged the NOTIFY.
.RE
.PP
.B NOTAUTH
.RS
The server is not authoritative for the zone.
.RE
.PP
.B NOTIMP
.RS
The server does not implement the NOTIFY opcode.
.RE
.PP
.B REFUSED
.RS
The server refused the NOTIFY request.
.RE
.PP
Errors (hostname resolution failure, network timeout, connection refused) are
reported on standard error and the script exits with status\ 1.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
NOTIFY sent and a response was received.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Requires Python\ 3.7 or later and the
.B dnspython
library (https://www.dnspython.org/). Install with:
.PP
.RS
.EX
pip install dnspython
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dig (1),
.BR named (8)
.PP
RFC\ 1996 \(em A Mechanism for Prompt Notification of Zone Changes (DNS NOTIFY)
.SH STANDARDS
RFC\ 1996
